# Keep the Docker build context to source + the FIDIR mirror.
#
# The Dockerfile copies whole trees (apps/, packages/, data/), so without
# these exclusions a local `docker compose build` / `pnpm release:dry-run`
# from a checkout that has been used with `pnpm dev` would bake client
# statement PDFs, exports and backups (DATA_DIR=./data) into an image
# layer, plus host node_modules / stale build output.

# VCS + secrets
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host dependencies and build output (the builder stage regenerates them)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
.turbo

# Runtime data written by dev runs — never ship it. The image only needs
# data/fidir (the mirrored FIDIR list).
data/uploads
data/exports
data/backups
data/tmp
tmp
apps/api/.tmp-backup-test

# Test / tooling artifacts
test-results
playwright-report
apps/web/e2e/.reachability.json
**/*.log
.claude
